Time Complexity: used to calculate the run time of algorithm
algorithm -> process or set of certain task
computation -> operation 
  time will be directly proportional to no of computation -> if computation increases time increases
  convergent -> many to one -> coming closer together
  divergent -> moving away from each other.

  time complexity can be calculated in 2 ways :
  1. math way -> Asymptotic 
  2. Experimental way -> 

1. Math way : (we can check our algorithm with experimental complexity)
  we have big O notation 
  we have big Omega notation 
  we have big teta notation

  so basically in graph , we have x axis -> no of inputs
  y - axis -> no of computation / timing
  meaning computation -> operation by cpu -> so timing is directly proportional to computation 
  if computation increases timing increases.
  
  calculation of run time should be with large no of inputs and divergent curve
  divergent : one to many -> convergent -> many to one curve
  
  worst case time complexity: tightest upper bond -> big O notation
  1. check closest to the head and divergent with large no of numbers
  
  best case time complexity: tightest lower bond -> big Omega Notation
  1. check the closest floor and divergent with large no of numbers.
  
  Avarage case time complexity -> big teta notation 
    sum of everythign / 2 will not work here, because worst and best cases will not have correct result , 
    the sweep area between is vary 
    Ex:
   inputs dependent algorithm -> based on the nature of inputs the time will very -> bubble sort
   input independent algorithm -> it doent care about inouts -> it will always stright line , 
   so all worst case and best case will be same line -> merge sort

  so the worst case and best case time complexity will be decided not only by experimental point or curve also sweep area.
  near top to sweep or near bottom to sweep (check image in phone) or  check the png in git - curve.png
